  "notes": "A 600-size electric helicopter, DIRECT DRIVE by the owner's preference: a huge slow outrunner (40 kV on 12S) bolted straight to the head, no gearbox anywhere - which is also exactly what the drivetrain model does. The tail rotor is a separate small brushless motor, as on the owner's real builds, so it keeps authority when the main motor is cut: convenient in the autorotation test and true to the aircraft. Two-blade head with a small flap-hinge offset and spring, so cyclic feels like an RC head rather than a teetering seesaw.\n\nEXPORT NOTES — contact spring numbers are Flightline-typical, not converted — the two contact models differ. drag CdA per axis estimated from the drag parts (x, 2x, 3x). tailRotor exported as the tail rotor (TtMax estimated 36.4 N).",
